  II. Trademark Notice

Fey™ and the Fey logo™ are trademarks of Aldo Zeroun. All rights reserved.


  II.A. Guidelines & Permissions

"Fey" and the Fey logo are trademarks representing the official Fey markup
language project. While our open-source software license governs the underlying
code, this trademark policy governs the use of our name and brand identity.

If you have questions regarding brand usage or wish to request permission for a
specific use case, please open an issue in the project repository.


  II.A.i. Permitted Uses (No Permission Required)

You are encouraged to use the Fey name and logo without prior written approval
in the following scenarios:

    *  Compatibility & Identification:
       You may use "Fey" in plain text to truthfully state that your software,
       plugin, tool, or library supports, parses, formats, or is written in the
       Fey markup language (e.g., "Fey plugin for Neovim", "A Fey-compatible
       parser in Rust").

    *  Community & Educational Content:
       You may use the name and logo in blog posts, tutorials, documentation,
       academic papers, and talks discussing or teaching the Fey language.

    *  Non-Commercial Reference:
       You may reference Fey to accurately link to the official project,
       repository, or specification.


  II.A.ii. Usage Requirements

When using the Fey trademark under these permitted uses, please adhere to these
guidelines:

    1.  No Implied Endorsement:
        Your use must not imply official sponsorship, affiliation, endorsement, or
        approval by the Fey project maintainers. 

    2.  Naming Distinction:
        Your project, repository, or package name must not use "Fey" as its
        primary name or lead brand. For example, use "Awesome-Tool for Fey"
        instead of "Fey Tool".

    3.  No Confusion:
        Do not use the Fey logo or name in a way that is likely to confuse users
        about whether your software or resource is the official implementation.

    4.  Distinction of Mark:
        Where practical, append the ™ symbol on the first or most prominent
        occurrence (e.g., Fey™ markup language).


  II.A.iii. Uses Requiring Prior Approval

You must obtain explicit written permission from the maintainers before using
the Fey trademark or logo in any of the following ways:

    *  Using "Fey" or the Fey logo as the main visual identity or brand of a
       commercial product, service, or company.

    *  Modifying, altering, or creating derivative versions of the official Fey
       logo for branding purposes.

    *  Registering domain names, social media handles, or trademarks containing
       "Fey" in relation to software, markup formats, or developer tooling.




